diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..08e9fbe 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -159,3 +159,27 @@ __Response:__
 ```
 
 `request` and `response` can be `null` for deliveries that have not started yet or are still in progress. The delivery request headers omit the `X-Webhook-Signature` header.
+
+## Deliveries
+
+When an event a webhook is subscribed to happens on its board, Fizzy posts to the webhook's `payload_url` once —
+each event is delivered to each receiver exactly once — and records the attempt in the delivery log.
+
+Requests carry these headers:
+
+| Header | Description |
+| --- | --- |
+| `User-Agent` | `fizzy/1.0.0 Webhook` |
+| `Content-Type` | `application/json`, or `text/html` for Campfire receivers |
+| `X-Webhook-Signature` | `HMAC-SHA256` of the request body, keyed with the webhook's `signing_secret` |
+| `X-Webhook-Timestamp` | When the event happened |
+
+The body is the JSON representation of the event, as shown by
+`GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks/:webhook_id/deliveries`. Receivers whose `payload_url` points at
+Campfire, Basecamp, or Slack get a readable chat message instead.
+
+Receivers are expected to answer with a `2XX` status. A receiver that fails ten times in a row within an hour is
+switched off: `active` becomes `false` and no further events are posted to it until it's reactivated with
+`POST /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks/:id/activation`.
+
+The delivery log keeps one week of history.
